The team adapted the key visual for social posts, app and web placements, posters, standees, floor signs, animation and in-store promotional materials (POSM). Each placement had a different job: a wide app visual could show several benefits, while a tall standee needed a clearer sequence for app download and the lucky draw.

My work was to translate the brief, coordinate feedback and carry the launch direction through those adaptations. The images above show the different crops, message priorities and calls to action; the design team owns the visual execution. The set of delivered formats is the output of that process.
